    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on favorable matchups today, with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining the offensive attack. Despite facing elite-tier arms, **Gunnar Henderson** (74.74) remains a must-start due to his role at the top of the order and a +16% park adjustment that helps offset the challenge posed by Gerrit Cole. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) finds himself in a high-leverage spot against Kyle Bradish; his projected #3 slot and significant park advantage provide a strong floor despite the xERA of 4.31. **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Heliot Ramos** (64.75) are also locked in as strong plays, with **Sam Antonacci** benefiting from a premium lead-off spot that maximizes his opportunities for the stolen bases we so desperately need to secure.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Nasim Nunez**, who finished just outside the starting rotation with a score of 36.77. While **Nasim Nunez** provides the elite sprint speed necessary for our SB-weighted strategy, the combination of a daunting matchup against Jacob deGrom and his assumed #9 position in the lineup severely throttled his efficiency score. Consequently, we opted to prioritize the plate appearances of **Coby Mayo** (45.87) and **Wade Meckler** (48.71) to ensure we don't bleed too much value in the remaining categories, though both are on thin ice given their scores. Note that several key roster pieces, including **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill**, are unavailable today due to injury or scheduling, placing extra pressure on our active starters to maintain our AVG and R/RBI output. Monitor the status of **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Coby Mayo** closely, as their scores are based on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions; any drop in batting order will require immediate re-evaluation of their daily utility.",
